pkg:Evidence_v1_7_2 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.7.2 (PATCH release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "PATCH: user pointed out the prior turn's close read covered Mission and jumped to Goal/Objective/Epic content, skipping a genuine re-examination of Scope itself -- correctly noting that isn't the actual BRSF chain order. Re-read CodeAbundanceScope's own hasScopeText fresh and found a real inaccuracy: it said 'keeping Stages 1-3 gate-clean,' but AreaAllStagesGateCleanliness explicitly covers all four stages including Stage 4's own gates -- the prose was never updated when the single-area scope was split into 3 areas two turns earlier. Rewrote it to represent all three areas as co-equal. Checked, rather than assumed, whether scopeRealizesObjective had the same single-objective gap as the Epic's pursuesObjective (fixed the prior turn): read its actual definition ('the objective this scope exists to achieve') and confirmed it is correctly narrow to the scope-facing objective specifically -- not a gap, verified rather than pattern-matched into an unnecessary fix. Re-read all Goal/Objective statement texts fresh against the currently-verified facts: internally consistent, nothing further found. Re-verified: pipeline order unaffected (digests track which individuals exist, not property values), full SHACL 0 violations."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "2f9cac7a3fd369d746c80700859ea93c0549d8f8b0b3dd5504ad6cf9b3974909"^^xsd:string .
